From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Merchant <john@johnmerchant.dev>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 13:15:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 53/53] hw/misc/chumby_io: Report the accelerometer and identity in
 the state query

A frontend resynchronising with the machine got the board's lines from
query-chumby-state, but the accelerometer's input and the identity only
from six qom-get calls. ChumbyState now also has accel-x, accel-y and
accel-z (milli-g) and guid, serial and hwversion, read from the
machine's properties of the same names; the acceleration comes from
the accelerometer itself, so a value set on /machine/accel shows too.

The identity is what the crypto processor and the DC ID EEPROM were
given when the machine was created. Setting it afterwards changed only
the machine's copy, so that is now refused, and the query cannot
report an identity the guest does not see.

The documentation gains a "Frontend interface" section: the machine
properties, the state query, the events, the input conventions and
screendump that frontends rely on, which will not change incompatibly
without a note there.

Signed-off-by: John Merchant <john@johnmerchant.dev>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01B1fN5Fc77Z6fVVe4rWJxPT
